## Atomic Design Rules

| Level | Contains | Examples |
|---|---|---|
| Atom | Single HTML element or primitive | Button, Input, Badge, StatusPill, Typography |
| Molecule | 2–4 atoms with a single purpose | FormField, SearchBar, SpecRow, ActionRow |
| Organism | Complex feature-complete unit | SpecCard, RefinementPanel, BacklogList, SessionTimer |
| Template | Layout structure, slots only | AppShell, TrayLayout |

- Atoms have no business logic and no data fetching
- Molecules may accept complex props but do not fetch data
- Organisms may use hooks (not TanStack Query — pass data via props or context)
- Data fetching lives in route loaders and query hooks in `apps/web`, not in `packages/ui`
